  "primary_subject_agency_ids": [],
  "summary": "River Forest, IL police Chief James Greenwood says the village will not cancel its ALPR contract with Minuteman Security Technologies, contrasting his department's system (Genetec hardware, Osprey software, sharing limited to 13 vetted Illinois agencies) with Flock Safety, whose contract Oak Park canceled Aug. 5 amid privacy and immigration-enforcement concerns. The article details River Forest's 44-camera network and plans to expand it.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "We will not cancel the contract with our vendor",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "We use a completely separate system with safeguards for data that exceed Flock's setup",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "Access to ALPR data is strictly limited to 13 vetted Illinois law enforcement agencies, all of which must be approved by the department.",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "In voting to cancel their contract with Flock, Oak Park trustees cited concerns over privacy, distrust of the Flock corporation and the potential for the cameras to be used for immigration enforcement",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    }
  ],
